  "decision": "Approved",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall begin not later than three years from the date of this decision.\r\nReason: In order to comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended by Section 51 of the Planning and Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and specifications: [202511-HB04, Unnumbered location plan, 202511-HB07. Received: 16/04/2025. 202511-HB02. Received: 24/04/2025. 202511-HB01. Received: 12/06/2025. 202511-HB03. Received: 20/06/2025].\r\nReason: In order to ensure the development is carried out in accordance with the planning permission.",
    "Condition : 3 - The hardstanding hereby permitted shall be made of porous materials, or include provision to direct surface water run-off to a permeable or porous area or surface within the application site, in accordance with the (then) Department for Communities and Local Government publication \"Guidance on the permeable surfacing of front gardens\" dated September 2008. The run-off shall not drain into any other foul or surface water drainage system.\r\nReason: In order to reduce surface water run-off and the associated pressure on local drainage systems and so prevent flooding. ",
    "Condition : 4 - Either side of the vehicle access hereby approved, visibility splay areas (the depth measured from the back of the footway and the widths outwards from the edges of the access, with a splay of at least 2.4 metres x 2.4 metres) shall be provided before the access and parking area is brought into use.  These areas shall be kept clear of any obstructions to visibility greater than 600 mm in height, including shrubs, planting, boundary walls, fences, gates, other means of enclosure or other structures or objects at all times.\r\nReason:  To ensure adequate visibility for drivers entering and leaving the site in the interests of pedestrian and vehicle safety."
  ],
